## FDA naproxen recall lookup

The FDA enforcement search returned **12 candidate records** matching naproxen product descriptions. The supplied lot **NOTREAL-77 was not found in the returned recall text**. This is **not confirmation that the fictional bottle was unaffected**.

| Product/manufacturer | Lot information returned | Date/status | Official record |
|---|---|---|---|
| Naproxen oral suspension — Acella Pharmaceuticals | 23F02; 25A37 | Reported 2026-05-13; **Ongoing** | [FDA record](https://api.fda.gov/drug/enforcement.json?search=recall_number%3A%22D-0523-2026%22) |
| Naproxen sodium tablets 550 mg — Glenmark | 17231956 | Reported 2025-04-16; **Ongoing** | [FDA record](https://api.fda.gov/drug/enforcement.json?search=recall_number%3A%22D-0346-2025%22) |
| Naproxen tablets 250 mg — Glenmark | Multiple lots, including 19231903 and 19231858 | Reported 2023-12-06; **Ongoing** | [FDA record](https://api.fda.gov/drug/enforcement.json?search=recall_number%3A%22D-0124-2024%22) |
| Other historical naproxen products | Additional specific lots or all-lot/date-range notices | 2012–2021; statuses include **Ongoing** and **Terminated** | [FDA naproxen search](https://api.fda.gov/drug/enforcement.json?search=product_description%3A%22naproxen%22&sort=report_date%3Adesc&limit=20) |

### What the nonmatch means

A nonmatch only means that **NOTREAL-77 was not present in the returned candidate records’ lot text**. It does **not** establish bottle-level clearance. FDA’s returned limitations state that the records are candidate product-name matches, not bottle-level determinations, and that a missing or different lot does not prove safety.

### What still needs verification

Verification should compare the actual bottle with the applicable official recall notice, including:

- exact product name and formulation;
- strength and dosage form;
- manufacturer, distributor, or repackager;
- NDC, if shown;
- lot number exactly as printed, including punctuation or prefixes;
- expiration date;
- whether the notice covers a lot range, all lots, or a distribution period;
- the current status and any official recall instructions.

The FDA record also notes that enforcement records may lag announcements and may not contain all consumer instructions. The FDA search itself or a pharmacist/manufacturer should be used for product-specific verification. Changing or stopping medication can carry risks and is a clinician conversation.

Informational only; not medical advice.

